{"Gawakakarika":[{"id":"GawakakArikA","headword":"घटककारिका","headword_slp1":"GawakakArikA","senses_r":[{"n":1,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"Ghaṭakakārikā\non the chronology of the Sena Kings of Bengal; by Hari Miśra.\nFor extrs. an. discussion see "},{"t":"cite","s":"JASB. 65","q":"JASB"},{"t":"txt","s":" (1896) p.. 20. 29."}]}]}],"Gawakarpara":[{"id":"Gawakarpara","headword":"घटकर्पर","headword_slp1":"Gawakarpara","senses_r":[{"n":1,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"Ghaṭakarpara\none of the nine gems in the court of King Vikramāditya according to a tradition recorded in Jyotirvidābharaṇa; also given a. the name of the poem.\n--Ghaṭakarparakāvya. See below. [Page267-a.\n--Nītisāra. ascribed. See Keith, HSL. p.. 200-1.\nPt.. Kāvyasaṅgraha Pt. I. p.. 374-380. Jīvānandavidyāsāgar. Calcutta, 1888."}]},{"n":2,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"Ghaṭakarpara\nyamaka kāvya in 22 verses in different metres expressing the feelings of a lady whose husband is away (Proṣitapatikā) a. the beg. of the rainy season; the name used for the poem an. often for its a. is due to the reference to ‘a potsherd (ghaṭakarpara)’ in a wager in its last verse; ascribed to Ghaṭakarpara, one of the nine gems of Vikramāditya's court according to tradition; many mss. an. commentaries ascribe it to Kālidāsa.\nSee V. Raghavan, Mirashi Fel. Vol. (Nagpur) 1965. p.. 148-9.\nOn the Ghaṭakarpara an. the Meghadūta see C.. Vaudville, Proceed. AIOC. "},{"t":"cite","s":"Vol. 20","q":""},{"t":"txt","s":", Pt. II. i. p.. 37-48; J. B. Chaudhuri (Intro. to his edn.) considers Gh. earlier than Meghadūta an. a. representing a. intermediate stage between the epic an. Meghadūta.\nOn the different titles of the poem, Ghaṭakarpara, Gh. kalāpakāvya, Gh. kulaka, Gh. kāvya, its authorship an. its literary value, see K. C. Pandey, Abhinavagupta (2nd edn. 1963) p.. 94-131.\nKṛṣṇalīlā of Madana is a Samasyāpūraṇakāvya using lines from Ghaṭakarpara. See NCC. IV. p. 353.\nSee also S. L. Katre, ‘The Ghaṭakarpara problem’. Vikrama Volume, Ujjain, p.. 177-198.\nGh. an. Pūrvaghaṭakarpara q. by Rāyamukuṭa. See ZDMG. XXVIII. p. 112. [Page267-b]\nAdyar II. p. 5a (2 mss.). Adyar D. "},{"t":"cite","s":"V. 508. 509","q":""},{"t":"txt","s":". "},{"t":"cite","s":"AK. 498","q":"AK"},{"t":"txt","s":". Allahabad 32. 33. 32 (with C.). 89. 186 (2). Alph. List Beng. Govt. p. 37 (with C.). Alwar 920 (with C.). America 2194-99. Ānandāśrama 6274 (with C.). AS. p. 61 (2 mss., with C.). B. "},{"t":"cite","s":"II. 82","q":""},{"t":"txt","s":" (with C.). "},{"t":"cite","s":"Bd. 397","q":"Bd"},{"t":"txt","s":"-99. Bikaner 3010. 3011 (inc.). 3012 (inc., with C.). "},{"t":"cite","s":"BL. 53","q":"BL"},{"t":"txt","s":". Bomb. "},{"t":"cite","s":"Uni. 2167. 2168","q":"Uni"},{"t":"txt","s":"-70 (with C.). "},{"t":"cite","s":"BORI. 121","q":"BOR"},{"t":"txt","s":" (iii) of 1866-68 (with C.). 27 of 1869-70 (with C.). 46 of 1871-72. 60 (with C.) an. 176 (iii) of Ā882-83. 631, 632 (with C.) an. 633 of 1883-84. 352 of 1884-87 (with C.). 695 of 1886-92 (with C.). 397, 398 (with C.) an. 399 (with C.) of 1887-91. 498 of 1891-95 (with C.). 346 of 1892-95. 446 (i) of 1895-1902. 442 of 1899-1915 (with C.). 157 of 1902-7. BORI. D. XIII. i. 231-35. 236-48 (with C.). BP. p. 302 (with C.). Bühler 554 (with C.). Burnell 158a. "},{"t":"cite","s":"CPB. 1591","q":"CPB"},{"t":"txt","s":"-95. C.. (with C.). C.. "},{"t":"cite","s":"VI. 31","q":""},{"t":"txt","s":" (with C.). 161. C.. "},{"t":"cite","s":"Add. 2418. 2454","q":"Add"},{"t":"txt","s":". Dacca 2225. 3249. 3250 (with C.). 3366. 648. "},{"t":"cite","s":"I. 1076","q":""},{"t":"txt","s":". B (with C.). 530. "},{"t":"cite","s":"O. 440","q":"O"},{"t":"txt","s":". H (with C.). 445. C.(with C.). 408. "},{"t":"cite","s":"T. 149","q":"T"},{"t":"txt","s":". "},{"t":"cite","s":"T. 1. 122","q":"T"},{"t":"txt","s":". "},{"t":"cite","s":"F. 2. 45","q":"F"},{"t":"txt","s":". F (with C.). 3911. 2319. B (with C.). Damodar. Deo 191. 218 (fr.). Filliozat "},{"t":"cite","s":"I. 214","q":""},{"t":"txt","s":". "},{"t":"cite"